2,1,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
3,1,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
4,1,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
5,1,1,talk,Asuka,,We need a structure that ensures stability without creating barriers for new members. I suggest we look at the actual costs and how people join.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"A prudent start. However, we must also consider the human cost of administration. A complex system is a burden on the treasurer.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. I think it is also important to understand how often members actually utilize the club's resources and who is doing the heavy lifting.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's not forget the vibe. If people are hesitating to show up, the fee structure might be part of the problem. We need to see who's actually coming.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Takumi,,I'm tired of guessing. We can't just pick a number and hope for the best like last time. We need hard data on what's actually coming in and going out.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, hard data is fine, but we must be careful not to make the process too transparent or rigid, as that might alienate the quieter members.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, transparency is a virtue, but efficiency is a necessity. I'm curious about the actual hours spent on the books.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Jonathan,,Perhaps we should look at the sign-in sheets and the rota. It would be helpful to see the gap between those who attend and those who don't.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,Exactly. I'm more interested in the patterns of attendance than the total numbers. Why are the regulars suddenly acting like guests?,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, hours are one thing, but the bank balance is another. If we don't know the exact renewal numbers, we're just flying blind again.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Asuka,,I'll focus on the mid-year joiners and the taster forms. We need to know why people choose to stay or leave.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,I shall investigate the treasurer's logged hours and the ledger of outgoings. Logic dictates we know the cost of both money and time.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Jonathan,,I will look into the tally of the sign-in sheets and the rota against the attendance record. I want to see the distribution of effort.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,I'll take the weekday turnout and the winter social notes. I want to see where the hesitation is creeping in.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Takumi,,"I'm taking the bank statements on last year's renewals and the ledger of outgoings. I won't let us set a fee based on a ""feeling.""","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
