30,2,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The data shows a clear trend. Newcomers are hesitant to commit to a full year's fee upfront. It's a significant barrier to entry.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"While that may be true, the administrative cost of ""flexible"" payments is staggering. The treasurer is spending entire evenings chasing small sums.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I've found that a very small group is carrying the entire weight of the club, both in attendance and labor. It feels unfair to charge them the same as those who never show.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It's not just about fairness, Jonathan. The ""pay-as-you-go"" mentality is killing the habit. People are weighing up the cost of every single visit.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"Listen, the fixed costs are seventy percent of our spending. Hall hire and insurance don't care if you're a ""regular"" or a ""guest."" We need a guaranteed base.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, if we prioritize the base over the newcomers, we'll stop growing. We need a way to let people drift in without a financial shock.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, ""drifting in"" is a luxury that the treasurer cannot afford. We are essentially asking a volunteer to work a part-time job as a debt collector.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"But if the regulars feel they are subsidizing the ghosts of the club, they will eventually burn out or leave. We need a tiered approach.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Tiers just add more mental math. The goal should be to make coming to the club a non-decision. You belong here, so you just show up.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, tiers are just more guesswork. If we don't cover the fixed costs upfront, we're risking the whole club's existence for the sake of ""fairness.""","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"I disagree. The ""non-decision"" you want, @Shunichi, is only possible if the entry fee is low. High upfront costs are a decision in themselves.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Let us be rational. A system that requires the treasurer to track individual session payments is a system designed for failure. It is unsustainable.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I'm not suggesting session payments, but perhaps a distinction between a ""supporting member"" and a ""basic member."" It acknowledges the effort of the regulars.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, that just creates a class system. ""I'm a supporting member, you're just basic."" It adds a layer of social friction we don't need.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"I don't care about the social friction. I care about the bank account. We have a massive fixed overhead that must be paid regardless of who is ""basic.""","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"We must find a middle ground. If we make the fee too visible or too rigid, we lose the very thing that makes this club a sanctuary.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,A sanctuary that is managed by a stressed-out volunteer is hardly a sanctuary. Simplicity is the only way to ensure the role remains fillable.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I simply believe that those who provide the labor and the presence should not feel exploited by those who pay a nominal fee and never appear.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,The real exploitation is making members feel like they are paying for a service rather than contributing to a community. We need to remove the friction.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Takumi,,Community doesn't pay the insurance. I'm not going to agree to any plan that leaves us guessing if we can afford the hall in six months.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
