59,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A is too high a barrier for newcomers. Option C is a nightmare for privacy and social flow. Option B is the only way to keep it accessible.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Option C is an absolute non-starter. It is the very definition of the administrative burnout I am concerned about. Option A is the only logical choice.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Option A ignores the imbalance of effort. Option B allows us to recognize those who are truly invested in the club's survival and daily operation.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option C turns every evening into a transaction. That's exactly why people are hesitating. Option A is the cleanest; you pay once and forget about it.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option C is a disaster waiting to happen. We'd be guessing our budget every single week. Option A is the only way to guarantee the fixed costs are covered.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, @Takumi, you are ignoring the taster forms. People are literally telling us they won't join because of the annual commitment. Option B solves this.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, the ""solution"" of Option B is merely shifting the burden from the member to the treasurer. More tiers mean more tracking and more confusion.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,Is the treasurer's convenience more important than the morale of the people actually running the events? Option B provides a sense of fairness.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Fairness is a trap here, @Jonathan. The ""fair"" thing is to make the club a place where you don't have to think about money once you've walked through the door.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"Exactly. And more importantly, Option A is the only one that gives us a predictable number. I won't vote for a system that relies on ""hope.""","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we choose Option A, we are effectively telling newcomers they aren't welcome unless they can commit a large sum upfront. That is a failure of our mission.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It is not a failure of mission; it is a reality of finance. A simple, flat fee is elegant, efficient, and prevents the treasurer from resigning in a month.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I still find Option A cold. It treats the person who does all the work and the person who never shows up as identical. Option B is a compromise.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, the ""coldness"" of a flat fee is actually a form of freedom. No tiers, no levels, no ""basic"" or ""premium."" Just members.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, we can't afford to be a charity. We have a hall to pay for. Option A is the only way to ensure we don't go bankrupt by mid-winter.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I cannot support a system that kills the club's openness. I will vote for Option B as the only viable compromise for growth and stability.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I shall vote for Option A. It is the only choice that respects the time of the volunteers and the logic of our fixed expenses.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will vote for Option B. We must address the resentment of the regulars before it becomes a permanent rift in the community.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'm voting for Option A. Let's stop overcomplicating this. Remove the psychological barriers and the administrative mess in one stroke.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Takumi,,Option A. I'm not gambling with the club's survival. We need the money upfront and we need it to be simple. No more guesswork.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
